# Ephemeral Claude agent worktrees (linked worktrees live under .claude/; each is a
# full repo copy — never track them from the parent worktree). Ignore everything
# under .claude/ EXCEPT the committed investigative-method skill layer, which is a
# tracked repo artifact (see docs/investigative-method/). Negate the directory (not
# a glob) so git descends into it; never negate .claude/worktrees.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches — centralized under .cache/ (configured in pyproject.toml)
.cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# uv
uv.lock.bak

# Node — one pnpm workspace (Epic #1549). The repo-root package.json holds dev tooling
# (markdownlint-cli2); web/ is a workspace member with its own node_modules. package.json
# files + the single root pnpm-lock.yaml ARE committed; node_modules (incl. the pnpm
# virtual store at node_modules/.pnpm) is not.
node_modules/

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data policy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source documents (scans, OCR PDFs, images) ARE versioned. Large binaries go
# through Git LFS (see .gitattributes); the reviewed structured extractions
# under data/extracted are the durable research artifact.
# Only regenerable working files are ignored:
data/cache/
data/scratch/

# Hearing audio is multi-GB and belongs in an evidence bucket, not git. The WAVs were
# externalized on 2026-06-10 (kept locally, pending upload); integrity + provenance are
# recorded in .../hearings-audio/hearings-audio-externalized.yaml. The derived transcripts
# stay committed.
data/documents/**/*.wav

# ── BEGIN vaulted corpus (generated from watermark.documents.vault; #2147) ──
# The source corpus lives in a yidam artifact vault, not in git (epic #2141). `git stores the
# record of them` is `data/*/*/vault.yaml`; the bytes are content-addressed in R2. Restore a
# working tree with `watermark documents hydrate`. Losing the vault costs no knowledge claim —
# every digest is in a commit — only the time to re-fetch.
#
# SUFFIX-SCOPED ON PURPOSE. #2147 proposed ignoring `data/documents/**` wholesale with a few
# re-includes; measured against the real tree that list was incomplete and would have ignored 725
# committed files — 191 `README.md` plus 534 others, including the 93 captured `.html`/`.htm` web
# evidence files, the `.index.yaml` passage indexes, `SOURCES.md`, geojson and csv. Naming the
# vaulted set instead touches exactly the 3,662 files that left, and needs no re-include list to
# go stale. It also sidesteps the trailing-`/*` trap documented further down: nothing here
# excludes a parent directory, so nothing needs re-including through one.
#
# ⚠️ GENERATED — these patterns ARE `VAULTED_SUFFIXES` + `VAULTED_EXTENSIONLESS`, and
# `test_the_gitignore_block_matches_the_vaulted_set` fails if they drift. Add a new source type in
# `watermark/documents/vault.py` and regenerate; editing only this block gets you a committed
# source byte that the manifests do not name.

# documents
data/documents/**/*.DOC
data/documents/**/*.JPG
data/documents/**/*.MOV
data/documents/**/*.MP3
data/documents/**/*.PDF
data/documents/**/*.PNG
data/documents/**/*.bmp
